  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light passing through a prism&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;suffers minimum deviation. It is found that the angle of incidence is double the angle of refraction within the prism. Then, the angle of prism is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><menclose notation=\"bottom\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></menclose></math>&nbsp;(in degrees).",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "60",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>At minimum deviation,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Also given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></math><br />Now&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>sin</mi><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>sin</mi><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>",
